--- A bulk insert the database refuses — rows that break a constraint, a
--- column the table lacks — answers an error value of kind 'db' with the
--- database's reason, as a statement the database refuses does (spec,
--- Fallible Builtins), and nothing of it is written. The compiled program
--- had unwrapped the answer and panicked, where the interpreter stopped
--- with the reason; dropped by its line, the failure now halts the program
--- as any value that failed does.
use db
use frame
c = connect['sqlite://:memory:']
query[c, 'CREATE TABLE t (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, v REAL NOT NULL)']

--- a key two rows share
twice = frame.new[id = [1, 1], v = [1.5, 2.5]]
n = insert[c, 't', twice]
log[n.ok]
log[n.reason]
log[n.kind]
log[len[query[c, 'SELECT id FROM t']]]

--- rows the table takes
log[insert[c, 't', frame.new[id = [5, 6], v = [1.5, 2.5]]]]
log[len[query[c, 'SELECT id FROM t']]]

--- a column the table lacks
odd = insert[c, 't', frame.new[id = [7], w = [1.0]]]
log[odd.ok]
log[odd.kind]

--- inside a function, handed back to its caller
fn put[c, rows]
    k = insert[c, 't', rows]
    return k + 1

log[put[c, frame.new[id = [8], v = [1.0]]]]
again = put[c, frame.new[id = [8], v = [1.0]]]
log[again.ok]
log[again.reason]

--- dropped by its line, the failure halts the program
insert[c, 't', frame.new[id = [8], v = [2.0]]]
log['not reached']
